# Machine-local settings for this checkout — COPY THIS TO .env
#
#     cp .env.example .env     # then edit
#
# Same split as config.yaml / config.example.yaml, and for the same reason:
# .env is gitignored, .env.example is committed, and nothing that describes
# ONE laptop ends up in the repository.
#
# config.yaml is for what the assistant DOES. This file is for where things
# ARE — paths and addresses that differ per machine. Nothing here is a secret;
# it is all "which computer is this".
#
# Everything is optional: each value below has a working default, and this file
# only overrides it. Shell launchers source it; Python reads it via os.environ.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where this checkout lives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The launchers (launch_hud.sh, assistant/jude/launch.sh) need an ABSOLUTE path
# and cannot reliably infer one: they are invoked by a .app bundle through
# `do shell script`, where the working directory is not the repo. They fall back
# to deriving it from their own location, which is right as long as they are
# still in the checkout.
#
# Set this if you keep the repo somewhere else, or run two checkouts at once.
#MACALENDAR_REPO=/Users/you/Desktop/Personal_Projects/MACalendar

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jude — the Judaic study assistant (assistant/jude/ARCHITECTURE.md)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jude is a separate repository and is not vendored here. `jude.path` in
# config.yaml is the usual place to point at it; this overrides that, which is
# handy when the checkout moves and you would rather not edit config.yaml.
#MACALENDAR_JUDE_PATH=/Users/you/Desktop/Personal_Projects/Torah_RAG

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API this machine serves
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The phone reaches the Mac at http://<tailnet-ip>:8080. The PORT is here; the
# ADDRESS lives on the phone, in MACalendar-iOS/Local.xcconfig (see
# MACalendar-iOS/Local.example.xcconfig) — it is a property of the client, not
# of this checkout.
#MACALENDAR_API_PORT=8080

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Stores, normally under ~/.assistant_tools/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every store honours an override; tests/conftest.py points all of them at a
# scratch directory. Set these only to run against a different set of real
# data — NEVER to point tests at the real ones.
#
#   MACALENDAR_DB, MACALENDAR_MEMORY_DB, MACALENDAR_VOCAB,
#   MACALENDAR_CATEGORIES, MACALENDAR_MODELS, MACALENDAR_LABEL_FEEDBACK,
#   MACALENDAR_MODEL_LOCK, MACALENDAR_DEVICE_SECRET, MACALENDAR_DEVICES,
#   MACALENDAR_TRACE_BUS, MACALENDAR_CHECKPOINTS, MACALENDAR_CONFIG
#
# CLAUDE.md's "Personal data lives outside the repo" explains why they exist.
